<programme start="20261118230000 +0000" stop="20261119010000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">Women&apos;s College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">South Carolina Upstate at Clemson</sub-title><desc lang="en">The South Carolina Upstate Spartans (4-1) play the Clemson Tigers (4-1) in a Division I game. South Carolina Upstate seeks to make it five straight behind guard Grace Booth, while Clemson beat Stetson 75-28 behind Mia Moore&apos;s points and assists.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191292_b_v12_bh.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261119010000 +0000" stop="20261119030000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Basketball</title><sub-title lang="en">Cornell at Syracuse</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Syracuse Orange (2-2) host the Cornell Big Red (2-2) at JMA Wireless Dome. Cornell fell to St. Bonaventure 88-64 and looks to Jacob Beccles, while Syracuse seeks to snap a two-game skid behind Kiyan Anthony, who leads the team in points.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Basketball</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191260_b_v8_az.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261119030000 +0000" stop="20261119060000 +0000" channel="ACCN ESPN"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Duke at Miami</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 7 Hurricanes (8-1, 6-0 ACC) try to recover as they host the Blue Devils (7-2, 4-2). Miami, which is without star wideout Malachi Toney, lost 31-24 at Notre Dame last week. Duke has won three straight after dismantling NC State, 41-3.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
