<programme start="20261120131400 +0000" stop="20261120150200 +0000" channel="AMC Thrillers"><title lang="es">The Other Man</title><sub-title lang="es">The Other Man</sub-title><desc lang="es">After his wife Lisa disappears on a business trip, Peter finds evidence that she has been having an affair with Ralph. He flies to Milan and enters into a complicated charade by befriending Ralph and slowly teasing information about Lisa out of him.</desc><credits><director>Richard Eyre</director><actor>Liam Neeson</actor><actor>Laura Linney</actor><actor>Antonio Banderas</actor><actor>Amanda Drew</actor><actor>Romola Garai</actor><actor>Laurence Richardson</actor><actor>Abigail Canton</actor><actor>Pam Ferris</actor></credits><date>20091215</date><rating><value>US_MPAA_R</value></rating><icon src="http://p-img.movetv.com/1280x720/e4b7566bb8d7715d590c86400c5e563c.jpeg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261120150200 +0000" stop="20261120165100 +0000" channel="AMC Thrillers"><title lang="es">The Last Thing Mary Saw</title><sub-title lang="es">The Last Thing Mary Saw</sub-title><desc lang="es">In the spring of 1840, a family gathers in their old, isolated farm house to mourn the loss of their matriarch. As the mourning proceeds, the circumstances of the matriarch&apos;s death come into question.</desc><credits><director>Edoardo Vitaletti</director><actor>Isabelle Fuhrman</actor><actor>Carolyn McCormick</actor><actor>Rory Culkin</actor><actor>Stefanie Scott</actor><actor>Shane Coffey</actor><actor>Judith Roberts</actor><actor>Michael Laurence</actor><actor>Tommy Buck</actor></credits><date>19010101</date><rating><value>US_MPAA_UR</value></rating><icon src="http://p-img.movetv.com/1920x1080/8ea9bbf12a8997d989839f8616e65d80.jpeg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261120165100 +0000" stop="20261120184200 +0000" channel="AMC Thrillers"><title lang="es">The Beta Test</title><sub-title lang="es">The Beta Test</sub-title><desc lang="es">A married Hollywood agent receives a mysterious letter for an anonymous sexual encounter and becomes ensnared in a sinister world of lying, murder and infidelity.</desc><credits><actor>Jim Cummings</actor><actor>PJ McCabe</actor><actor>Virginia Newcomb</actor><actor>Kevin Changaris</actor><actor>Olivia Applegate</actor><actor>Jessie Barr</actor><actor>Christian Hillborg</actor><actor>Malin Barr</actor><actor>Jacqueline Doke</actor><actor>Wilky Lau</actor></credits><date>20211105</date><rating><value>US_MPAA_UR</value></rating><icon src="http://p-img.movetv.com/1920x1080/90658dcc5ff016b90e72e5e2452ca07d.jpeg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261120184200 +0000" stop="20261120202500 +0000" channel="AMC Thrillers"><title lang="es">Dog Eat Dog</title><sub-title lang="es">Dog Eat Dog</sub-title><desc lang="es">Three ex-cons (Nicolas Cage, Willem Dafoe, Christopher Matthew Cook) find themselves on the run from the mob and the police after botching a plan to kidnap a baby for a large ransom.</desc><credits><director>Paul Schrader</director><actor>Nicolas Cage</actor><actor>Willem Dafoe</actor><actor>Christopher Cook</actor><actor>Louisa Krause</actor><actor>Omar Dorsey</actor><actor>Melissa Bolona</actor><actor>Rey Gallegos</actor><actor>Chelcie Melton</actor></credits><date>20161104</date><rating><value>US_MPAA_UR</value></rating><icon src="http://p-img.movetv.com/1920x1080/ad3037d6f64a70f2acfd454ffca38f7d.jpeg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261120202500 +0000" stop="20261120221600 +0000" channel="AMC Thrillers"><title lang="es">The Owners</title><sub-title lang="es">The Owners</sub-title><desc lang="es">An elderly couple turn the tables on a group of young thieves who broke into their house while they were away.</desc><credits><director>Julius Berg</director><actor>Maisie Williams</actor><actor>Sylvester McCoy</actor><actor>Rita Tushingham</actor><actor>Jake Curran</actor><actor>Andrew Ellis</actor><actor>Ian Kenny</actor><actor>Stacha Hicks</actor></credits><date>19010101</date><rating><value>US_MPAA_UR</value></rating><icon src="http://p-img.movetv.com/1920x1080/a962989d870309aa5dae0442a33833a5.jpeg"/></programme>
